# CYS-YNA-mod2-alkyne — alternative mod2 for the alkyne pre-Michael input case
#
# When the user uploaded a ligand with the C≡C still drawn (the free drug
# SMILES form, e.g. CC#CC(=O)N1CCC[C@@H]1... from PubChem), this mod2 block
# REPLACES the default `data_mod_CYS-YNA-mod2` in CYS-YNA.cif. It encodes
# the Michael-addition chemistry that the bond declaration triggers:
#
#   (1) Change Cα≡Cβ from triple to double bond
#   (2) Add H on Cα (Michael addition transfers one H to the α carbon)
#   (3) Retype Cα and Cβ from sp to sp2
#   (4) The new SG–Cβ bond is added via the link's bond block (not here)
#
# Selected at runtime when the SMARTS detector matched either:
#   CYS-YNA-pre          (internal alkyne, R-C≡C-C(=O)-N)
#   CYS-YNA-pre-terminal (HC≡C-C(=O)-N, Spebrutinib-class)
#
# For the terminal-propiolamide case (R = H, no Cγ on the warhead), the
# JS detector additionally appends one extra _chem_link_angle row to the
# link block:
#   1 SG 2 <CB> 2 <HCB-new> 118.0 3.0
# (the H ends up where the methyl would have been; see plan-doc §A.3.)
#
# PLACEHOLDER TOKENS substituted at runtime (same set as CYS-YNA.cif):
#   <CB>  ← Cβ atom-id   (e.g. C19 in XQQ)
#   <CA>  ← Cα atom-id   (e.g. C13)
#   <HCA> ← H to add on Cα (named to match ligand's existing H-naming
#            convention, e.g. H13 if the ligand uses C-numbered H atoms)
#
# References:
#   ~/Moorhen/docs/covalent-ligand-plan.md Appendix A.2
#   ~/Moorhen/docs/refs/nicholls-modelling-2021.pdf §3.1 (chem_mod semantics)

data_mod_CYS-YNA-mod2

# (1) Change Cα≡Cβ from triple → double
loop_
_chem_mod_bond.mod_id
_chem_mod_bond.function
_chem_mod_bond.atom_id_1
_chem_mod_bond.atom_id_2
_chem_mod_bond.new_type
_chem_mod_bond.new_value_dist
_chem_mod_bond.new_value_dist_esd
 CYS-YNA-mod2 change <CB> <CA> double 1.34 0.02

# (2) Add a new H on Cα (named to follow the ligand's H-naming convention)
# (3) Retype Cα and Cβ from sp to sp2 (energy-type CR1 = sp2 vinyl carbon)
loop_
_chem_mod_atom.mod_id
_chem_mod_atom.function
_chem_mod_atom.atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_symbol
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_energy
_chem_mod_atom.new_partial_charge
 CYS-YNA-mod2 add    <HCA> <HCA> H HCH1 .
 CYS-YNA-mod2 change <CA>  .     C CR1  .
 CYS-YNA-mod2 change <CB>  .     C CR1  .
